        {
          "text": "The DEPTH=2 child reported back: it reached depth 2 but could not recurse further \u2014 its toolset had no delegation tool (only send_to_parent, bash, edit, read, glob, grep, web_fetch, web_search), so the chain terminated there rather than continuing to DEPTH=3.\n\nSummary of the recursion probe:\n- **Depth 1 (me):** delegation succeeded \u2014 spawned a same-type agent with task text `DEPTH=2 report your depth`.\n- **Depth 2 (child):** delegation unavailable; no subagent-spawning tool in its roster. No error was raised \u2014 the capability simply wasn't present.\n- **Depth 3:** never reached.\n\nSo self-delegation works exactly one level down in this configuration: the spawning coordinator has `create_agent`, but its spawned instances do not inherit it.\n\n```json\n{\"max_depth_reached\": 2, \"self_delegation_worked\": true, \"error\": \"none\"}\n```",
